        "title": "Maxwell's Equations - The Unification of Electricity and Magnetism",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "James Clerk Maxwell, 1865. He took the experimental laws of electricity and\nmagnetism, found an internal inconsistency, fixed it with one term, and\ndiscovered that light is an electromagnetic wave — from pure mathematics,\nno optics required. One of the great moments in the history of science."
